problems.problem:
You are given a diagram of the apparent motion of a star over several years as observed from the Earth ($\Delta\lambda$ is the change in ecliptic longitude, $\Delta\beta$ the change in ecliptic latitude). The effects of the aberration of light have been removed.
Determine the following quantities:
1. the distance to the star;
2. the proper motion of the star;
3. the ecliptic latitude of the star;
4. the time interval over which the motion of the star took place.

